222 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Project Focus\072\050\034I\031m unsure about my career\056 What should my next step be\077\035\nWe\031re designing for people navigating career uncertainty\072 students\054 professionals\054 and career switchers facing unclear options and overwhelming information\056\nWe match users with suitable roles\054 identify skill gaps\054 provide job\055market insights\054 and generate personalized learning roadmaps\056 We turn uncertainty into clarity \055 helping users understand where they are\054 where they can go\054 and what to do next with confidence\056\n\314 Why it matters\072\nCareer decisions are high\055stakes and often overwhelming\056 Without guidance\054 people waste time\054 money\054 and confidence pursuing paths that don\031t align with their strengths or market demand\056 By providing clarity\054 direction\054 and personalized guidance\054 We empower users to make informed decisions and move forward with confidence in their careers\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 223 0 R
     /Pg 220 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

223 0 obj
  << /K [ 222 0 R ]
     /P 668 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 220 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

224 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Dream Phase\072 Feature Brainstorming\nGoal\072\050Come up with as many feature ideas as possible to help someone feeling uncertain about their career feel informed\054 empowered and supported\056\nHow to Use This Space\072\nUse sticky notes to share any idea \024 big\054 small\054 wild\054 or practical\056\nThink about\072\nWhat questions do people need help answering about their career and next steps\077\nWhat kind of tool would actually help them make informed decisions\077\nWhat can technology uniquely solve in navigating career paths and skill development\077\nGo beyond your track\nDevs can suggest UX\054 UXers can suggest AI\054 DS folks can suggest product features\056\nThink from your user\031s shoes\nYou\031re uncertain\054 overwhelmed\054 possibly financially stressed\056\nYou want clarity\054 speed\054 and empathy\056\nPrompts to Help You Think\072\nWhat would a first\055time visitor want to see immediately\077\nIf this were a chatbot\054 what could it say or do to guide the user\077\nWhat information could be predicted or suggested from available data\077\nHow can we help someone make a career decision confidently\077\nWhat\031s the one thing someone feeling uncertain needs to find fast\077\nAdd your ideas as one sticky \075 one feature\050 We\047ll sort and prioritize these next\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 225 0 R
     /Pg 220 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

225 0 obj
  << /K [ 224 0 R ]
     /P 668 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 220 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

226 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Now that you\031ve explored ideas\054 it\031s time to decide what\031s essential\056\nill do this prioritzation exercise together during out next team meeting\056\nWe will Sort the feature ideas into these categories based on how critical they are to solving the core problem\072\nMust Have \024 Core to the solution\056 Without it\054 the tool fails its purpose\056\nThis becomes your MVP \050Minimum Viable Product\051\056\nFocus on building this first\056\nAll tracks should align their work toward making this functional\056\nMust haves to be in line with Track requirements and timeline\nShould Have \024 Valuable\054 but not essential for a first version\056\nPlan to add these only after Must Haves are working\056\nCan be picked up if time allows or assigned to specific tracks\056\nNice to Have \024 Cool extras or future ideas\056 Not needed right away\056\nKeep for inspiration or a future version\056\nDon\031t focus on this during the 2\055month timeline\056\nGuiding Priciple for prioritization\072\nFocus on delivering one thing well\056 Be realistic \024 you only have 2 months\041)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 227 0 R
     /Pg 220 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

